message: >-
  If you use this software or its results in your research, please cite
  it as follows (and, for data and protocol details, the referenced
  publication).
title: "rietveld-agent: reproducible laboratory-scale Rietveld quantitative phase analysis"
abstract: >-
  An open, deterministic toolkit for validating, refining and reporting
  Rietveld quantitative phase analysis (RQPA) of laboratory powder X-ray
  diffraction data, demonstrated on the four NIST SRM 2686a reference
  patterns. GSAS-II is the numerical authority; the repository provides a
  versioned, staged refinement protocol, a COD-pinned structure set, and
  an honest-uncertainty reporting layer.
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-08-11"
license: Apache-2.0
keywords:
  - powder X-ray diffraction
  - Rietveld refinement
  - quantitative phase analysis
  - SRM 2686a
  - cement clinker
  - reproduction
